 "scenes": [
  {
   "id": "intro",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A max-heap gives the largest key fast, but finding the smallest means searching every leaf. Some problems need both ends. The min-max heap answers both, in one array, with the same logarithmic costs. This video builds one."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "head"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Min-max heaps"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Here are the seven stages."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "stages"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Why we want both ends, the alternating levels, and finding the minimum and maximum."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[0..=2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Then inserting, deleting from both ends, and an exam question."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[3..=6]"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "why",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 1: a double-ended priority queue removes either its smallest or its largest item. One ordinary heap makes only one end fast."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 1 of 7: both ends"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "stages"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "de"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "de[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Two heaps, one min and one max, work, but every key is stored twice and deletions must be mirrored in the other heap."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "de[0][2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A min-max heap does it in one array. It is used for the extremes of a sliding window, or a bounded buffer that may drop its best or its worst entry."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "de[1..=2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "one structure, both extremes"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "levels",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 2: the shape is a complete binary tree in an array, as before. The order is new: the levels alternate."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 2 of 7: min and max levels"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "de"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "lv"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "lv[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Even levels, starting with the root at level 0, are min levels: a node there is at most every key below it."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "lv[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Odd levels are max levels: a node there is at least every key below it."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "lv[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "So the order runs between a node and its grandchildren, two levels apart, and that is how the algorithms move."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "lv[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "even levels min, odd levels max"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "find",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 3: this min-max heap, from Horowitz and Sahni: 7 at the root, 70 and 40 below, then 30, 9, 10, 15, then 45, 50, 30, 20, 12."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 3 of 7: min and max"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "lv"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "t0"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The root, on a min level, is at most everything: the minimum is 7."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "mark",
       "target": "t0.h1"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The maximum lies on level 1: the larger of the root's two children. 70 against 40: the maximum is 70. Both found in constant time."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "t0.h2"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "t0.h3",
       "delay": 0.3
      },
      {
       "action": "mark",
       "target": "t0.h2",
       "delay": 0.6
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "min = A[1] · max = max(A[2], A[3])"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ins",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 4: insertion. Put the key at the next free position, then compare it with its parent to decide which kind of levels it must climb."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 4 of 7: inserting"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "t0"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "ir"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ir[0..=2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Then climb two levels at a time, swapping with the grandparent while out of order. One path, every other level: O of log n."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ir[3..=4]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Insert 5. It lands at position 13, below 10. Position 13 is on level 3, a max level, but 5 is smaller than its parent 10, which sits on a min level. So 5 belongs on the min levels."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "ir"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "t5"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "t5.h13"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Swap it with the parent: 5 moves to position 6. Then climb the min levels: its grandparent, the root, holds 7. 5 is smaller, swap. 5 is the new minimum."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "t5.h13",
       "value": "10"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "t5.h6",
       "value": "5",
       "delay": 0.1
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "t5.h6",
       "value": "7",
       "delay": 0.5
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "t5.h1",
       "value": "5",
       "delay": 0.6
      },
      {
       "action": "mark",
       "target": "t5.h1",
       "delay": 0.8
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Insert 80 instead. It lands at position 13, below 10, on a max level. 80 is larger than its parent, so it stays on the max levels and climbs by grandparents: the grandparent, 40 at position 3, is smaller, so swap. Position 3 has no grandparent. 80 is the new maximum."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "t5"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "t80"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "t80.h13"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "t80.h13",
       "value": "40",
       "delay": 0.4
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "t80.h3",
       "value": "80",
       "delay": 0.5
      },
      {
       "action": "mark",
       "target": "t80.h3",
       "delay": 0.8
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "parent decides the side, grandparents do the climbing"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
